            "result": "Copied all 14,206 tracker attachments into the helpdesk with their original timestamps and authors, and proved none was lost.\n\n## What was made\n\n- `scripts/copy_attachments.py`: copies every attachment from the old tracker into the matching helpdesk ticket, keeping the author and upload time.\n- `scripts/checksum_both.py`: compares a SHA-256 of every file on both sides and writes `reports/checksums.csv`.\n- `reports/summary.md`: counts per project, the 3 h 10 min run, and the 14,206 of 14,206 matching checksums.\n\n## How to use it\n\n1. Set `TRACKER_TOKEN` and `HELPDESK_URL` in `.env` (see `.env.example`).\n2. Run `python3 scripts/copy_attachments.py --dry-run` to see what would move.\n3. Run it without `--dry-run`, then `python3 scripts/checksum_both.py` to prove the copy.\n\n## Key files\n\n- `scripts/copy_attachments.py`\n- `scripts/checksum_both.py`\n- [reports/summary.md](../reports/summary.md)\n\n## Limits\n\n- The old tracker stays read-only; nothing was deleted there.\n- Attachments added to the old tracker after 2026-10-15 are not copied; rerun the script to pick them up.\n",
